From: Perry Raskin <perryraskin@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: sio: refuse unowned inherited J86 remap

The running J86 retained remap-enable=1 with CPU control=0. A stopped
CPU is insufficient ownership evidence. Refuse before firmware allocation
or writes; no mapping takeover/restore policy has been qualified.

--- a/drivers/soc/apple/apple-sio-core.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/apple-sio-core.c
@@ -873,6 +873,14 @@
 			return dev_err_probe(sio->dev, ret ?: -EBUSY,
 					     "SmartIO CPU is already running\n");
 	}
+
+	/* A stopped CPU does not make an inherited firmware mapping ours.
+	 * Live J86 retains remap-enable=1 even with CPU_RUN clear. Until a
+	 * reviewed remap lease/restore protocol exists, do not overwrite it. */
+	if (sio->legacy_a7 &&
+	    readl(sio->base + apple_sio_reg(sio, APPLE_SIO_REMAP_ENABLE)))
+		return dev_err_probe(sio->dev, -EBUSY,
+				     "J86 inherited SIO remap is not owned by this driver\n");
 
 	/* No user-helper fallback: a missing image must not stall the boot. */
 	ret = request_firmware_direct(&firmware, firmware_name, sio->dev);
